{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F} = \\Ker(\\mathcal{K}^n \\to \\mathcal{K}^{n + 1})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-K-flat-flat-acyclic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fdc294de679420e1dcb6f27ac25769acc0ca66d3948ec083b2d63285b4a43b52", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2c6b7d60e81691621aa05c26c8d4e026308a1b42f0923f2a33f8b106c109187a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a K-flat, acyclic complex with flat terms. Then\n<MATH_0003>\nis a flat <MATH_0004>-module.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5af6677a79481087e93cf28c43a5ef8838c1df13ba6cc66db67b05750c59f918", "unit_id": "tag:0G7C:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\ldots \\to \\mathcal{K}^{n - 2} \\to \\mathcal{K}^{n - 1} \\to\n\\mathcal{F} \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Tor}_i(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^\\mathbf{L} \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\mathcal{K}^{n - 3} \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{G} \\to\n\\mathcal{K}^{n - 2} \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{G} \\to\n\\mathcal{K}^{n - 1} \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{G}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\text{Tor}_1(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{G}) = 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-bounded-flat-K-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-flat-tor-zero}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34b214e8f07477040ed8f3fa041aea43eac1edadc83c10e49b1b95f02bede057", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d5b229dda94bffded0eabeba407cc1a3d150be981e50cb37b21b2cee5c9fe7ba", "source_text": "Observe that\n<MATH_0001>\nis a flat resolution of our module <MATH_0002>. Since a bounded above complex\nof flat modules is K-flat (Lemma <REF_0001>)\nwe may use this resolution to compute\n<MATH_0003> for any\n<MATH_0004>-module <MATH_0005>. On the one hand\n<MATH_0006>\nis zero in <MATH_0007> because <MATH_0008> is acyclic\nand on the other hand it is represented by\n<MATH_0009>.\nHence we see that\n<MATH_0010>\nis exact. Thus <MATH_0011>\nand we conclude by Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:412cfc04ec247c572a7bf4537d0a06077be9402b2efd3c79968ead34b5df83e3", "unit_id": "tag:0G7C:proof"}
